# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Template for local environment variables. COMMITTED ON PURPOSE.
#
# Setup:
#   cd frontend
#   cp .env.example .env.local
# then fill in the values. .env.local is gitignored -- never commit
# it, and never put real values in this file.
#
# This file lives in frontend/ because Vite only loads env files
# from its own project root (the folder containing vite.config.js).
# A .env at the repo root would be silently ignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# !! EVERYTHING BELOW IS PUBLIC !!
#
# Vite inlines every VITE_-prefixed variable into the JavaScript
# bundle shipped to the browser. Anyone can read these in devtools.
# The prefix is a deliberate opt-in to publication, not a secret
# store. Only put values here that are safe to publish.

# Supabase project URL and anonymous key.
# The anon key is designed to be public, but it is ONLY safe if
# Row Level Security is enabled with policies on every table.
# Without RLS, this key grants the whole internet read and write
# access to your data.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Google Maps JavaScript API key.
# Before using this, restrict it in Google Cloud Console to an
# HTTP referrer allowlist (localhost plus your deployed domain)
# and to the Maps JavaScript API only. An unrestricted key lifted
# from the bundle can be used to run up charges on the billing
# account.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-SIDE SECRETS DO NOT BELONG IN THIS FILE OR ANY .env HERE.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY must never reach
# the browser. They are set on the Supabase Edge Function runtime:
#
#   supabase secrets set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...
#
# This is why the AI hint feature has to run in an Edge Function:
# the browser calls the function, and the function calls Anthropic.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
